.TH MD4X 1 "August 2026" "" "General Commands Manual"
.nh
.ad l
.
.SH NAME
.
md4x \- convert Markdown to HTML, plain text, JSON, ANSI or normalized Markdown
.
.SH SYNOPSIS
.
.B md4x
.RI [ OPTION ]...\&
.RI [ FILE ]
.
.SH DESCRIPTION
.
.B md4x
reads a Markdown document from \fIFILE\fR \(em or from \fBstdin\fR(3) when no
\fIFILE\fR is given, or when it is \fB-\fR \(em converts it, and writes the
result to \fBstdout\fR(3) unless \fB--output\fR names a file.
.PP
The Markdown dialect is fixed and cannot be selected: CommonMark, plus the
GitHub extensions (tables, task lists, strikethrough, permissive autolinks,
alerts), plus md4x's own (LaTeX math, YAML frontmatter, Comark/MDC components,
inline attributes, highlight, footnotes). There are no per-extension switches.
Raw HTML in the input is passed through unsanitized.
.PP
A \fB--\fR argument ends option processing; the remaining argument, if any, is
taken as \fIFILE\fR. Only one input file may be given.
.
.SH OPTIONS
.
.SS General options:
.
.TP
.BR -o ", " --output= \fIOUTFILE\fR
Write output to \fIOUTFILE\fR instead of \fBstdout\fR(3). \fB-\fR means
\fBstdout\fR(3).
.
.TP
.BR -t ", " --format= \fIFORMAT\fR
Output format, one of:
.RS
.IP \fBhtml\fR 12
HTML (the default). Only the \fB<body>\fR contents, unless \fB--full-html\fR is
given.
.IP \fBtext\fR 12
Plain text, with all markup stripped.
.IP \fBjson\fR 12
The document as a Comark AST in JSON.
.IP \fBansi\fR 12
Terminal output with ANSI escape sequences.
.IP \fBmarkdown\fR 12
Clean, normalized Markdown \(em frontmatter, raw HTML and component props are
dropped, and the surviving syntax is re-emitted in one spelling.
.IP \fBheal\fR 12
The healed Markdown \fIsource\fR, not a rendering of it: unclosed emphasis,
code spans, fences, links and the like are completed. See \fB--heal\fR.
.RE
.
.TP
.B --heal
Heal incomplete Markdown \(em typically a partial stream from a language model
\(em before rendering it, so that unterminated markup does not derail the
output. Applies to every format; with \fB--format=heal\fR the healed source
\fIis\fR the output and this option adds nothing.
.
.TP
.BR -s ", " --stat
Measure time of input parsing (reported on \fBstderr\fR(3))
.
.TP
.BR -h ", " --help
Display help and exit
.
.TP
.BR -v ", " --version
Display version and exit
.
.SS HTML output options:
.
These apply to \fB--format=html\fR and are ignored for every other format.
.
.TP
.BR -f ", " --full-html
Generate full HTML document, including header
.
.TP
.B --heading-ids
Add a generated \fBid="..."\fR anchor to every heading. The id is a
GitHub-compatible slug of the heading text, de-duplicated within the document
\(em the same id the \fBjson\fR output publishes. Off by default, so plain
output matches CommonMark.
.
.TP
.B --html-title= \fITITLE\fR
Sets the title of the document (with \fB--full-html\fR)
.
.TP
.B --html-css= \fIURL\fR
Add a CSS link (with \fB--full-html\fR)
.
.SS Development options:
.
.TP
.B --replay-fuzz
Treat the input as a fuzz test case: the first four bytes are read as the
renderer-flag word and the rest as the document. Internal debugging aid; it is
not listed by \fB--help\fR.
.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.
.TP
.B 0
The document was converted successfully.
.
.TP
.B 1
An error occurred: an unknown option or output format, more than one input
file, an input or output file that could not be opened, an input larger than
4294967295 bytes, or a failed conversion. Diagnostics are written to
\fBstderr\fR(3).
.
.SH EXAMPLES
.
.TP
.B md4x README.md
Render a file to HTML on standard output.
.
.TP
.B md4x -t text README.md
Strip the markup and print the plain text.
.
.TP
.B cat README.md | md4x -t json -o out.json
Read standard input and write the Comark AST to a file.
.
.TP
.B md4x -f --html-title=Docs --html-css=style.css -o out.html README.md
Write a complete HTML document with a title and a stylesheet link.
.
.SH SEE ALSO
.
https://github.com/unjs/md4x
.
